🎓 Key Learnings: Anatomy of a Tool
The Decorator (@tool): Intercepts standard Python functions and formats them into JSON-schema-compatible tools that LangChain models can recognize.

Type Hints: Explicitly defines parameters (str) so the LLM knows precisely what arguments to provide.

The Docstring: Acts as the "prompt" for the LLM. Because the model never sees your raw code, a precise docstring directly impacts whether the model selects and executes the tool correctly.

